Parity unit : page:automations/AutomationsList   kind=page   web route=/automations
Web source  : web/src/features/automations/pages/AutomationsListPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) + Windows App SDK / WinUI workload — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (generated-client data adapter), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7
  ApiLogsPage / FeedbackQueuePage do. The generated prompt's idealized
  "AutomationsListPage.xaml + AutomationsListPageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Automations" is mapped onto
  these real conventions; the surface registers itself with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("Automations",
  already in RouteTable.cs → /automations) in ShellWindow.xaml.cs, wiring its NavigationRequested event to the
  shell NavigateTo (web navigate('/automations/new') Create / empty CTA).
- Data binding (ADR-004): the 8 manifest data sources are useAutomations (GET /automations), useAutomationHistory
  (GET /automations/history?limit), useVehicles (GET /vehicles), usePinned (GET /pinned?type=automation),
  useToggleAutomation (PATCH /automations/{id}/toggle), useReEnableAutomation (PATCH /automations/{id}/re-enable),
  useDeleteAutomation (DELETE /automations/{id}) and useTestRunAutomation (POST /automations/{id}/test-run). The
  view-model reads/writes through an injected IAutomationsListFeed; the default EmptyAutomationsListFeed resolves
  the empty state (matching the ApiLogsPage/FeedbackQueuePage host-injection precedent), and the generated-client
  AutomationsListClientFeed (AutomationsListPage.Source.cs) binds to the generated OpenAPI operations
  (get_api_v1_automations, get_api_v1_vehicles, get_api_v1_pinned [type=automation], get_api_v1_automations_history
  [limit], patch_api_v1_automations_id_toggle {enabled}, patch_api_v1_automations_id_re_enable,
  delete_api_v1_automations_id, post_api_v1_automations_id_test_run, post_api_v1_automations_import) and is asserted
  in tests via the FakeApiClient. No HTTP touches the view.
- Status/search filtering and pin ordering are client-side (web filteredItems → sortedItems): the projection mirrors
  computeStats, the active/disabled/auto-disabled predicates, the name/description search, and floats pinned ids to
  the top in pin order. Each surviving automation is projected into the shared AutomationCard's AutomationCardModel
  (vehicle scope label resolved from useVehicles, pin flag from usePinned). The recent-activity feed reuses the
  shared AutomationActivityFeed leaf, fed the history slice + summary; live SSE events are out of scope for this
  page (no SSE hook in the manifest data sources) so it composes with an empty live-event set.
- The collapsible Quick-Start-Templates panel (web <details> wrapping <PresetGallery/>) hosts the shared
  PresetGalleryView, wired to the page's default (empty) preset source so the gallery renders its own empty branch
  until a real presets read is injected — mirroring the page's EmptyAutomationsListFeed default.
- The typed-import handler is faithfully reproduced: the view opens a .json FileOpenPicker (the web file input),
  the pure AutomationImportEnvelope.IsValid gate rejects untyped/legacy exports (web isAutomationImportEnvelope)
  before POST /automations/import, and failures surface in a ContentDialog using the localized import strings.
- SI units N/A (no unit-bearing fields on this surface). All 23 i18n keys resolve through the ILocalizer facade
  with the web key names; 6 previously-absent keys were added to Strings/en/Resources.resw
  (translation.automations.autoDisabledWarning, .empty.cta, .filters.all, .importFailedWithReason,
  .importTypedEnvelopeRequired, .noMatch.cta); the other 17 already existed verbatim.

